Hello all,

I have a number of bird species for which I ran NMix models using the pcount function.  Result from my models were a mixed bag, partially stemming from low detectability.  I wish to report out the model fits (good and bad) but I was not quite clear on the best way to interpret the output from my goodness of fit tests (parboot, Nmix.gof.test)on the global models.  Through readings on this group and in the Applied Hierarchical Modeling in Ecology test, I think I grasp the bullet points about dispersion and p-values, but was hoping someone here might be generous enough to offer some further clarity or point to some more resources.  Here are some example values from my GOF outputs:

species

mixture

p-value

c-hat

BCCH

P

0.587

0.987772

BTNW

P

0.999

0.839083

OVEN

P

1

