TUTI

P

0.911

0.94141

Most discussion that I have seen notes that p-vals <.05 could be interpreted as significant, and the model has either poor fit or under/over dispersion depending on the value of c-hat. But what about p-values of 1 or close to it?  I have a few species where this is the case, and most are paired with c-hat values <.8.  Is this indicative of significant underdispersion and/or lack of fit?  Furthermore, does anyone have any rough cut off point for when underdispersion is “too great” and the model should be rejected (if at all)?

Thanks

Cal

